Subject: [PATCH milos-linux v1 0/1] Input: eswin_eph861x: double-tap wake
To: Jorijn van der Graaf <jorijnvdgraaf@catcrafts.net>

Make double-tap-to-wake work with the EPH8621 touch controller on the
Fairphone 6. The vendor LP (gesture) path was compiled out, so a
selected gesture never reached the controller. This adds a small
generic-PM port of it and an lp_mode attribute so a display-power
daemon can arm gestures while the panel is blanked.

The patch follows the existing file's (vendor) 4-space indentation, so
checkpatch reports indentation errors; the driver is not mainline yet.

Tested on the Fairphone 6 with the panel blanked (system awake).
System suspend with a gesture selected is untested.

Development was assisted by an AI coding tool (see the Assisted-by tag).

Paul Schuldesz (1):
  Input: eswin_eph861x: Support double-tap wake through generic PM and
